rep('''- **Prompt** (`prompts/synthesis/synthesis-v1.md`).''','''- **Prompt** (`prompts/synthesis/synthesis-v2.md`, schema `synthesis-output-v2`; ruling 17). v2 adds, for format compliance and the ruling 17 and 18 rules: the reply starts with `{` and ends with `}`; every claim but DESCRIPTIVE has at least one values entry (the schema requires it with `if`/`then` and `minProperties`); every number written is in values under its fact name and is named next to its measure; window names and year ranges in the text are the claim's window; rank numbers only in RANKING claims with `rank.<k>.storedRank` and `rank.<k>.researcherId`; PATH_HOP claims carry all five hop facts; DESCRIPTIVE claims have no number, at most one researcher name, and no relationship; summary and uncertainty follow the same rules. `synthesis-v1` stays loadable (`RuntimeSchemas.SynthesisOutputVersions`) until configuration selects v2 (domain-engineer, section 20), and the non-empty values rule is enforced in code for both (`Synthesis.problems`).''')
