rep('''Key-value reads in the CLI use `cli.ItemFileIndex` (a read-only offset index over the item files, items read on demand and validated when indexed), not `InMemoryDynamo`: the full item fake beside the full graph fake runs out of memory at `-Xmx6g` (measured in work order 4). Tests use `InMemoryDynamo`.''','''Key-value reads in the CLI use the storage `ItemFileReader` (STORAGE.md "Indexed item-file reader"; ruling 22, review 1 F6), not `InMemoryDynamo`: the full item fake beside the full graph fake runs out of memory at `-Xmx6g` (measured in work order 4). The rag-side `ItemFileIndex` is deleted. Tests use `InMemoryDynamo`.''')
rep('''Work order 4 tests place injection strings (including the text seen in an OpenAlex response, noted for the threat model) in the question, in a rendered document, and in a researcher name and a paper title, and assert that the plan operations, the store calls (template IDs and bound IDs), and the verified claims do not change.''','''Work order 4 tests place injection strings in the question, in a rendered document, and in a researcher name and a paper title, and assert that the plan operations, the store calls (template IDs and bound IDs), and the verified claims do not change. Repair-01 (`InjectionSpec`, ruling 21): the fixture text holds `<`, `>`, `&`, `"`, and the closing tag of every delimiter (`</question>`, `</graph_evidence>`, `</semantic_context>`, `</notes>`, `</item>`, `</doc>`) in the question, W2's title, the display name of a fixture researcher, and a profile document; an injected question goes through the model planner and the synthesis prompt builders with a recording fake model; each built prompt has exactly one opening and one closing tag per block and the escaped forms; and the plan operations, store calls, and claims equal those of the clean question. Removing the escaping in `Planner.promptValues`, `Synthesis.promptValues`, or `EvidenceBuilder.render` makes a test fail. The OpenAlex injection text is not available, so that requirement is waived (ruling 21, m3); the threat model (Phase 17) records the waiver.''')
